<h1>Home lab notes</h1>
<p>Working notes on a small home network: a router, a NAS, a couple of Raspberry Pis and too many cables.
Nothing here is polished; these are reminders to myself.</p>
<h2>Backups</h2>
<p>Nightly <code>restic</code> snapshots of the NAS to an external drive, weekly check with
<code>restic check --read-data-subset=5%</code>. Restores tested once a quarter.</p>
<h2>Monitoring</h2>
<p>Uptime probes every minute, alerts only after three consecutive failures. Anything noisier gets ignored anyway.</p>
<h2>Reading list</h2>
<ul>
  <li>RFC 9000 (QUIC) sections 5–7</li>
  <li>The systemd hardening options man page, <code>systemd.exec(5)</code></li>
  <li>Notes on BBR vs CUBIC on lossy links</li>
</ul>
